---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Flashcards & Anki deck
description: Every key term and concept from the System Design Guide as flashcards. Play them on a pocket console in the browser, or download the Anki deck.
section: flashcards
permalink: /flashcards/
---
{%- set groups = collections.topics.concat(collections.practice) -%}
<div class="home">
  <p class="eyebrow">Review</p>
  <h1>Flashcards &amp; Anki deck</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ flashcards.length }} cards covering every fundamental and practice question in the guide. Play them on the handheld below, or import the deck into <a href="https://apps.ankiweb.net/">Anki</a> for spaced repetition.</p>

  <div class="fc-play">
    {#- The console. guide.js drives the screen; buttons carry data-key. -#}
    <div class="gb" data-gb>
      <button class="gb__sh gb__sh--l" type="button" data-key="left" aria-label="L: previous topic"></button>
      <button class="gb__sh gb__sh--r" type="button" data-key="right" aria-label="R: next topic"></button>
      <div class="gb__power" aria-hidden="true"><span class="gb__led"></span>POWER</div>

      <div class="gb__wing gb__wing--l">
        <div class="gb__dpad" role="group" aria-label="Direction pad">
          <button class="gb__d gb__d--up" type="button" data-key="up" aria-label="Up: scroll up">▲</button>
          <button class="gb__d gb__d--left" type="button" data-key="left" aria-label="Left: previous topic">◄</button>
          <span class="gb__dc" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <button class="gb__d gb__d--right" type="button" data-key="right" aria-label="Right: next topic">►</button>
          <button class="gb__d gb__d--down" type="button" data-key="down" aria-label="Down: scroll down">▼</button>
        </div>
        <div class="gb__ss">
          <span class="gb__sskey"><span>START</span><button class="gb__round" type="button" data-key="start" aria-label="Start: play or menu"></button></span>
          <span class="gb__sskey"><span>SELECT</span><button class="gb__round" type="button" data-key="select" aria-label="Select: next topic"></button></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="gb__face">
        <p class="gb__maker" aria-hidden="true">Sagun</p>
        <div class="gb__bezel">
          <div class="gb__screen" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Flashcard screen" aria-live="polite">
            <div class="gb__meta" data-gb-meta></div>
            <div class="gb__body" data-gb-body><p>Loading…</p></div>
            <div class="gb__hint" data-gb-hint></div>
          </div>
          <p class="gb__logo" aria-hidden="true">STUDY BOY<span>ADVANCE</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="gb__wing gb__wing--r">
        <div class="gb__ab">
          <span class="gb__key gb__key--b"><button class="gb__btn" type="button" data-key="b" aria-label="B: again"></button>B</span>
          <span class="gb__key gb__key--a"><button class="gb__btn" type="button" data-key="a" aria-label="A: flip, then got it"></button>A</span>
        </div>
        <div class="gb__speaker" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="fc-side">
      <h2 id="how-to-play">How to play</h2>
      <ul class="fc-keys">
        <li><b><span class="arw">◄ ►</span> L R SELECT</b><span>Pick a topic (or all of them).</span></li>
        <li><b>START</b><span>Start the deck. Press again mid-game for the menu.</span></li>
        <li><b>A</b><span>Flip the card. Once you've read the answer, A means <em>got it</em>.</span></li>
        <li><b>B</b><span><em>Again</em>: the card comes back a few cards later.</span></li>
        <li><b><span class="arw">▲ ▼</span></b><span>Scroll a long answer.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fc-note">Keyboard, after clicking the console: arrow keys, <kbd>X</kbd> = A, <kbd>Z</kbd> = B, <kbd>Enter</kbd> = START, <kbd>Shift</kbd> = SELECT.</p>
      <div class="fc-field">
        <label for="gb-cart">Cartridge (topic)</label>
        <select class="fc-select" id="gb-cart" data-gb-cart>
          <option value="">All topics ({{ flashcards.length }} cards)</option>
          {%- for p in groups %}
          {%- set n = (flashcards | cardsFor(p.data.cards or p.fileSlug)).length %}
          {%- if n %}<option value="{{ p.data.cards or p.fileSlug }}">{{ p.data.navTitle or p.data.title }} ({{ n }})</option>{% endif %}
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="fc-actions"><button class="fc-sound" type="button" data-gb-sound aria-pressed="true">♪ Sound: on</button></div>
    </div>

    <div class="fc-side">
      <h2 id="anki">Anki deck</h2>
      <div class="fc-actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/assets/anki/system-design-guide.apkg" download>Download .apkg</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/assets/anki/system-design-guide.csv" download>CSV</a>
      </div>
      <p class="fc-note">In Anki: <b>File → Import</b> and pick the <code>.apkg</code>. Cards are tagged by topic (for example <code>sdg::caching</code>), so you can study one area at a time. Importing a newer version updates cards instead of duplicating them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="all-cards">All cards</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">Click a card to flip it.</p>
  {%- for p in groups %}
  {%- set cs = flashcards | cardsFor(p.data.cards or p.fileSlug) %}
  {%- if cs.length %}
  <section class="fc-topic" id="{{ p.data.cards or p.fileSlug }}">
    <h2><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.data.navTitle or p.data.title }}</a></h2>
    <div class="cards">
      {%- for c in cs %}
      <button class="card" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="card__front">{{ c.front | md | safe }}</span><span class="card__back">{{ c.back | md | safe }}</span></button>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</div>
<script id="deck" type="application/json">{{ flashcards | deckJson(groups) | safe }}</script>
